.TH AGENT-HOOK-STOP 1 "2026-10-14" "agentguard" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
agent-hook-stop \- run end-of-turn agent checks and notifications
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B agent-hook-stop
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B agent-hook-stop
reads a stop hook JSON payload from standard input, asks Hive Memory for any
pending-memory reminder, runs its extensions, and plays a terminal notification
(naming the agent process with
.BR "term-notify-sound \-\-owner" )
for the first Stop after a valid prompt that ends the foreground turn. A Stop
an extension blocks to keep the agent working stays silent, so the Stop that
later ends the turn rings although the runtime flags it as a continuation.
Other re-entrant and repeated callbacks stay silent until another valid prompt
re-arms the shared AgentGuard state. A Stop that dies before deciding, because
an extension crashes or exits, or a host timeout sends HUP or TERM, still ends
the turn and rings unless the hook had already emitted a block. A SIGKILL
timeout (OpenCode sends one) cannot ring. On Codex, the
Hive Memory check and notification still run, but the response is replaced
with empty JSON and the hook exits 0: Stop continuations are suppressed because
affected Codex releases persist their synthetic messages with replay-invalid
item IDs. Prompt-submit still surfaces memory reminders before Stop. On Grok,
the response is always empty JSON because Grok treats Stop context as
keep-working feedback; an extension block still exits with status 2.
.PP
A foreground Stop that lets the turn end also clears the agent's busy tmux
pane mark with
.BR "term-pane-mark clear busy" .
A subagent Stop, or one an extension blocks to keep the agent working, leaves
the mark set; because Codex Stop is always fail-open, an extension block does
not keep it on Codex, nor on a runtime that declares
.BR AGENTGUARD_STOP_BLOCK_ENDS_TURN .
Such a Stop also rings. Only the pane terminal's foreground agent changes the
mark, so the Stop of an agent it launched, which runs without that terminal,
leaves it alone. A Claude Code interrupt fires no Stop or other turn-ending
hook, so after one the mark stays set until the next prompt's turn ends or the
session ends.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AGENTGUARD_STOP_BLOCK_ENDS_TURN
Set to
.B 1
by a runtime adapter whose runtime logs this hook's exit status 2 and ends the
turn anyway (the OpenCode adapter does). A blocked Stop then counts as the end
of the turn.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The turn may stop normally.
.TP
.B 2
On runtimes other than Codex, the hook asks the agent runtime to continue
because a block must be surfaced.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR agent-hook-notification (1),
.BR hm (1),
.BR term-pane-mark (1)
